WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.600
So last night was the second and final presidential
debate.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.800
And I have to tell you, for me, being so desensitized
to this stuff being so used to what we see

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.669
and hear from politicians, it is actually
an outlier.

00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:17.330
It really is a debate that was superlative
compared to other debates in a number of different

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.330
ways.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.710
Number one, Joe Biden did really well.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:23.679
I didn't expect Joe Biden to come out in the
way we did.

00:00:23.679 --> 00:00:28.060
I knew he would say things that would make
sense, but I didn't imagine that he was going

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.619
to be from a tone and optics perspective.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:35.550
So strong in comparison to Donald Trump.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:42.020
I also didn't imagine that Donald Trump was
going to come out almost despondent and barely

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.930
able to even respond to Joe Biden's attacks
for the first 70 percent of the debate, the

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:51.890
last 30 percent going to conspiracy theories
and saying things that don't make any sense.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:55.559
And it was one of the most uneven debates
I can imagine watching.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:01:03.039
I thought back to 2012, the famous Obama Romney
debate where Romney made kind of a fool out

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:07.530
of himself, starting to say things that didn't
make sense and then trying to get Obama to

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.530
concede something.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:12.240
And Obama just sitting there casually saying,
please proceed, Governor.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.320
And it was very uneven.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.570
But Romney's performance was better than Trump's
last night.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:23.710
And Joe Biden just landing brutal hit after
hit on Trump.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:30.650
Trump seemed almost slowed down, depressed,
confused, looked like he was taking physical

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:35.049
punches rather than simply metaphorical ones
in the first debate.

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:38.950
Biden wasn't nearly as strong as I'd like
to see.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:45.009
And Trump was kind of annoying with his childish
interruptions, but it was not so lopsided.

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:48.250
Last night's debate stunningly one sided.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.030
